From ab9592ef91fb66791ad577a10f524cd88ff8db2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:06:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: lay foundation for one-workspace-one-client worker
 architecture

Phase 1 of the client-workspace/worker restructure: audit and split
tooling to enforce one live engagement per workspace (dry-run by
default, guarded behind --execute), a unified worker registry merging
Showtime's and Reputation Manager's separate skill manifests into one
catalog for future Library/enablement UI to iterate, and an explicit
enabledAt column + evidence-based resolver so "enabled" has one
unambiguous meaning per client without touching the existing
dispatch-gating convention any cron/poller already relies on. The
combined Work sidebar's Capabilities grid now shows only a client's
actually-enabled workers instead of the full catalog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
